You shine like a diamond

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:07,660
You shine like a diamond

28
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:14,760
Let's turn back time for a moment

29
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:26,860
Poor girl

30
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,320
Damn those magic knights

31
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:33,420
What's her condition?

32
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,220
She appears to have cracked several ribs

33
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:38,900
Shall I prepare some pain medication?

34
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,380
Yes, you could use some

35
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:45,040
Here you are

36
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,140
Thanks, I appreciate it

37
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,800
Here, drink

38
00:02:48,800 --> 00:03:01,540
The pain should eventually subside

39
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:02,780
Okay

40
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:06,920
So what should our next move be?

41
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:15,140
Master Kabwe?

42
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:17,260
What exactly do you plan to do?

43
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,240
I'm going to kill the prisoner

44
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,760
No, not yet!

45
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,760
There are more important things that we need to worry about right now

46
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,580
Like that book?

47
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,500
It needs to be dealt with too

48
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,880
Lest our sacrifices be in vain

49
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,180
Wait, dealt with how?

50
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:35,460
They say that the devil dwells in the five-leaf clover

51
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:38,900
Let us be rid of this accursed book at once

52
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,100
Master Kabwe, please!

53
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:41,880
Why are you trying to stop me?

54
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,380
This wretched thing

55
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,560
It couldn't possibly be of further use to us

56
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,460
Wait

57
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:52,560
I don't really care about what you do to me

58
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,640
But Austin needs that book

59
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,580
So give it back

60
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,800
What a selfless request

61
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:01,260
But when such words come from lips tainted by forbidden magic

62
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,540
Well, I'd be a fool to listen

63
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:10,100
Siona, what's going on?

64
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:17,420
Siona, is she dead?

65
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,560
Onabi!

66
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:34,460
No

67
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:38,720
Damn you

68
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,880
Why betray us?

69
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,460
Have you still not put it together?

70
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,240
I'll say it plainly

71
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:52,300
The last thing we would want is to see the devil banished

72
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:56,540
We are the devil believers

73
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,760
We are an order that worships the devil

74
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,160
That can't be true

75
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,740
How can anyone worship such pure evil?

76
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:08,880
No

77
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,840
You asked us to help you destroy the devil

78
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:12,700
If not that

79
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,800
And what did you need us for?

80
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,520
You speak like we came to you as supplicants in need

81
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:21,600
But we simply took advantage of your hatred for the devil

82
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,260
In what way?

83
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,520
Well, seeing as you have access to the magic parliament

84
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:29,680
You've been privy to knowledge that was kept from us peasants

85
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:33,820
In addition to that, it's helpful to have someone who can actually use magic

86
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,680
Since we're dealing with the magic knights

87
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,780
Someone who can use magic?

88
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:40,060
What are you talking about?

89
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,860
Right

90
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:45,600
For somebody like you, it must be difficult to fathom

91
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:48,040
That there are people like us

92
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:50,280
Who are all but spurned by mana

93
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:53,900
One hot summer day

94
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:57,340
The neighborhood kids asked me to do a favor for them

95
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:07,780
They asked me to use my catalyst magic

96
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:10,180
To mix both of their magics together

97
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:12,960
So we could all cool off

98
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:25,020
They seemed truly happy

99
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:28,400
And seeing their faces made me feel happy too

100
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:41,600
But then I overheard them talking behind my back

101
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:45,960
And they said they were only acting like my friends to impress the adults

102
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,300
Since I didn't have any real friends

103
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:52,900
They said it was because I could barely use magic

104
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:54,400
She's so creepy

105
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:57,280
Then they just laughed

106
00:06:57,280 --> 00:07:01,420
People like us have no place in this kingdom

107
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,640
We've been told that since we were children

108
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:07,440
You think this will help you?

109
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:08,740
We do

110
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:11,240
Before now, it's been like we didn't even exist

111
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,900
But no more

112
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:17,140
Despite the fact that he doesn't have a single drop of magic in his blood

113
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:21,360
Asta wields power equal to that of any great mage

114
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:24,080
By means of a grimoire that hosts a devil

115
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,800
So we'll imitate him

116
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:30,200
We'll do whatever we must to obtain the devil's might for ourselves

117
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:33,280
I will not allow that to happen

118
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:38,240
Why you?

119
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:53,120
Let's go

120
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,600
Right?

121
00:07:54,600 --> 00:08:07,800
No

122
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:11,080
I can't let it end like this

123
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,620
I'll find a way

124
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:16,860
We're listening

125
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:18,520
Where are you?

126
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:24,100
It's a lie

127
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:28,200
These people aren't trying to bring about the devil's demise

128
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,240
Not at all

129
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,160
The truth is that

130
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:35,640
They're after the devil's power

131
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,980
What do you mean?

132
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:42,860
This organization actually worships the devil

133
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:46,920
They're called devil believers

134
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:50,020
Chairman Damnazio

135
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:51,400
I'm sorry

136
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,140
I was a fool

137
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:55,540
You must stop them

138
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:56,980
Please, sir

139
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,820
For all of us

140
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:02,240
What's wrong, Cobway?

141
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:02,640
Report

142
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:08,660
Do you mind filling us in on the details?

143
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,720
A devil-worshipping cult, huh?

144
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,420
Called the devil believers?

145
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:20,540
I don't think your subordinates would help that kind of group knowingly

146
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:23,920
It's safe to assume that they were being used under false pretenses

147
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:26,120
Those gullible idiots

148
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:29,260
I get wanting to destroy a devil

149
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,760
But who the hell would decide to worship one?

150
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,740
These people are a bunch of sickos, if you ask me

151
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:38,520
Excuse me

152
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:42,060
We traced the communication magic back to its source

153
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:43,720
And it would appear to have come from Tulio

154
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,560
Well, that's a surprise

155
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:47,460
Julius?

156
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,780
I order the Black Bulls to travel to Tulio

157
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:53,600
Apprehend these devil believers

158
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,760
And save Nero from their clutches

159
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:58,580
You got it

160
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:09,580
He must have used the last of his strength

161
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,900
To grab that thing so he could contact his former boss

162
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,640
Was it an argument gone bad?

163
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:16,520
No, there'd be signs of a struggle

164
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,940
These guys didn't have a chance to fight back

165
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,200
So they just slaughtered their own people?

166
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,520
It's like Chairman Chinmole said

167
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,060
They were being played for fools

168
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:27,260
They thought they were fighting a devil

169
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:30,000
Guess they must have outlived their usefulness

170
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,660
Captain

171
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:34,420
So creepy

172
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:37,320
A venomless viper

173
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,620
Powdered long-necked soft-shell turtle

174
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:41,780
And the root of a goikabuto plant

175
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:44,920
These ingredients are all quite difficult to come by

176
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,580
And knowing that

177
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,900
We can assume that the potion

178
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,860
Which put my best friend Asta to sleep

179
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:51,920
Was likely made here

180
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:54,980
As were the potions used at the execution site

181
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:57,760
I would love to get more information

182
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,280
On the person who lives here

183
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,180
But the local villagers

184
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:03,240
Seem to be pretty wary of us

185
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:06,880
I can help you with that, sir

186
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:10,960
Granny Maggie?

187
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,200
It's me

188
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,780
Oh, hi, Gordon

189
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:16,280
You brought some friends, eh?

190
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,100
This is Granny Maggie, everyone

191
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:19,120
We got to know each other

192
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:21,300
And became friends the last time we were here

193
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,860
How goes it, Granny?

194
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,420
My name is Asta, ma'am

195
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,540
It's an honor to meet you

196
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:27,300
You're way too loud

197
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,300
So are you, Magna

198
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,500
Hold on

199
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,380
Where's that mean-looking boy

200
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:32,440
Who called me an angel?

201
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,620
Don't tell me you came all this way

202
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:35,720
And didn't bring him

203
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,140
An angel?

204
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:39,960
Oh, if you mean my best friend, Ghosh

205
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:41,340
He's back at the capital

206
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,760
Watching over his little sister

207
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:45,560
Ah, well, it's a relief to hear

208
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,260
He was able to find the poor girl

209
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,380
Right?

210
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:51,020
I hate to rush this cute little reunion

211
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,220
But can we pick your brain for a bit, Granny?

212
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:57,640
We need info on the person who lives in the forest on the outskirts of town

213
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,680
You're talking about Bo?

214
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:00,920
Yeah, probably

215
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,400
We need you to tell us everything you know about Bo

216
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,500
It's real important

217
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:05,600
I can do that

218
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,220
But the next time you come around

219
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:10,640
You bring that broody young ghost fellow with you

220
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,340
Oh, you got it

221
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:15,580
She can barely use magic?

222
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:18,280
It's not actually all that rare

223
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,840
Though, I bet it seemed that way to you, Noelle

224
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,500
You can't really blame her

225
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:25,660
I mean, every single member of her family is good at magic

226
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,720
And Asta can't use it at all

227
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,120
And she knows he's a freak

228
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,820
This is all your fault

229
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:31,640
My fault?

230
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:32,720
But

231
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:36,340
Bo is also a wonderfully skilled apothecary

232
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:40,760
We don't go to a mage with recovery magic when we fall ill in this town

233
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:45,340
Herein tool you the sickling goes straight to Bo with her expertly made medicine

234
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:48,340
I could tell she was skilled just by looking at her shelves

235
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:51,340
I hear she worked hard to become that good

236
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,760
Perhaps we're all lucky she couldn't use magic

237
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:56,760
Because that's what drove her to develop such a skill

238
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:59,340
Kind of sounds like a certain meathead I know

239
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:06,340
Come to think of it, you might want to hear about Bo's good friend Dozzy

240
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:11,340
She lost both her husband and mother-in-law when those devil servants attacked the town

241
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:13,340
Where can we find her?

242
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:19,340
Like Bo, Dozzy can't really use magic

243
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,340
But she never let that get her down

244
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:24,340
She's a wonderful girl who's been through a lot

245
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:27,340
You'd better be nice to her if you meet

246
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:30,340
She got along very well with her husband V-Day

247
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:34,340
The two of them were as happy as any couple I've seen

248
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:40,340
Her husband's mother, Meishu, would always talk about what a wonderful daughter-in-law she was

249
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,340
Yami!

250
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:43,340
Hmm?

251
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:45,340
I think you should take a look at this, sir

252
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:50,340
This woman

253
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:58,340
Oh yeah, I've seen her before

254
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,340
Something's not right about this

255
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,340
Well, think about it

256
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:07,340
The old lady was just going on and on about how Dozzy and her husband were deeply happy

257
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:10,340
But that face looks pretty dead inside

258
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:13,340
Hang on

259
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:22,340
Why would someone whose family was killed by a devil become one of the creeps who worships a devil?

260
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,340
Nice work

261
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:28,340
You're on the right path, just keep flipping over rocks until you find some worms

262
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,340
Yeah, about that

263
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,340
Honestly, I have my doubts

264
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,340
And why is that?

265
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:35,340
The trail's getting kind of cold is all

266
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:38,340
I don't suppose you have any other intel we can go off of?

267
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:41,340
Nothing solid

268
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:47,340
I will say that the devil believers sought out people with the magic parliament in hopes of getting sensitive information from them

269
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:52,340
With that in mind, they likely know that the devil Megicula is in the spade kingdom

270
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:55,340
And that information probably factors into their plans

271
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:58,340
So what, you think they might want to offer Nero as a gift?

272
00:14:58,340 --> 00:14:59,340
Huh

273
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:02,340
That reminds me, they still have the kids' grimoire too

274
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:04,340
How could you forget something that important?

275
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:05,340
Right

276
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:09,340
They probably wanted to give you and the grimoire to Megicula as some kind of package deal

277
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:13,340
Once they pay tribute, they'll defect to the spade kingdom

278
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,340
Or rather the devil inside it

279
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:17,340
Okay, but why?

280
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:21,340
I doubt we can answer that question without asking these people in person

281
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:26,340
But in any case, we can expect these cultists to start moving north

282
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:30,340
To reach the border, they'll have to cut across the Forsaken realm

283
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,340
Right, good luck

284
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,340
Thanks

285
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,340
Look sharp, dumbasses

286
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:39,340
We're moving out

287
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:40,340
Yes, sir

288
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,340
A mission?

289
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:44,340
That's right

290
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:45,340
I can't

291
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:50,340
Neglecting your duties, you must enjoy disappointing your sister

292
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:51,340
Old hag

293
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:53,340
Just what do you think you're doing here?

294
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,340
I think you know

295
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:58,340
I'm here to rescue Marie from her obsessive good-for-nothing brother

296
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,340
No, my angel stays here

297
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:03,340
What happened to her before was a fluke

298
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:05,340
I can guarantee Marie's safety now

299
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:08,340
Now get over yourself and go do your job

300
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:09,340
Shut your mouth, old hag

301
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:12,340
There's no job that's more important than watching over Marie

302
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:16,340
And have you given any thought to what would make Marie happy?

303
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:20,340
Magic knights are supposed to keep people safe, right?

304
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:24,340
I was so proud when I found out my big brother was going to be a magic knight

305
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:26,340
But I want to keep being proud of you

306
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,340
So please, Ghosh

307
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:33,340
I'll listen to you this time, but don't get used to it

308
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:37,340
I'm trusting you, so you had better not put Marie in danger again

309
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:42,340
Get your ass over here

310
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:45,340
She'll be safe with me

311
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:59,340
And so, the black bulls began their pursuit of the devil believers

312
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:02,340
Who had thought to have fled into the forsaken realm

313
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,340
In case this thinking had been an error

314
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:09,340
The other magic knight squads were sent out to search the common realm far and wide

315
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:13,340
But no matter how diligently the magic knights searched

316
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:16,340
They had no luck finding the devil believers

317
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:20,340
And several days passed with no progress

318
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:24,340
We've trekked through half the forsaken realm chasing these jerks

319
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:27,340
But we haven't caught so much as a whiff of their mana yet

320
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,340
It's possible that they're using some kind of devices to keep their mana concealed

321
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:35,340
The other squads haven't found anything noteworthy either

322
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:38,340
At this point, I would assume they've passed the forsaken realm

323
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:41,340
And are bound for the spade kingdom's border

324
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,340
Sounds about right

325
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,340
We've come across a few signs that they passed through ahead of us

326
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,340
Signs?

327
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,340
Yeah, bunch of weird crap

328
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:54,340
The locals at this village are not a whiff of their mana yet

329
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:57,340
It's possible that they're using some kind of devices to keep their mana concealed

330
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:02,340
The locals at this village say a bunch of their people disappeared too

331
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:04,340
It's happening everywhere we go

332
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:07,340
Do you think these devil whatevers are behind it?

333
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:10,340
That'll be my guess until I hear a better one

334
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:14,340
Hey, I got a question for you guys

335
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:20,340
Why the hell is everybody so determined to avoid us?

336
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:23,340
It's due to what happened with the eye of the midnight sun

337
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:24,340
Huh?

338
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,340
The people of the forsaken realm have had it quite rough

339
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:30,340
Almost everyone here feels like the magic knights left them high and dry

340
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:34,340
And at least a few of these people believe that the magic knights were behind the attacks

341
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:37,340
I'll do what I want

342
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,340
You can't make me stay

343
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,340
Please don't do this

344
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:45,340
Stop trying to keep me here, you've already made me late to the meetup

345
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,340
Everyone else is already there, I have to leave right now

346
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:51,340
You think they'll heal your leg with the devil's power?

347
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,340
Do you know how ridiculous that sounds?

348
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:55,340
Why would you think that's possible?

349
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,340
I don't think it is, I know it is

350
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,340
I mean, there's a guy who doesn't have any magic at all

351
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:04,340
And with the devil's powers he was able to get into the magic knights

352
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:07,340
But the boy was put on trial for using those powers

353
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:09,340
What do I care?

354
00:19:10,340 --> 00:19:12,340
Once I have the devil's powers, I won't have to be scared of trials or anything else

355
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:14,340
Now let me go!

356
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:17,340
No, don't! Someone stop him, please!

357
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:21,340
What the? Hold it right there!

358
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:25,340
Hey, you had better explain why your mother's on the ground, now!

359
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:28,340
Just let go of me, I have to leave right now, no matter what!

360
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,340
They're all waiting for me just outside of town

361
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:39,340
Yep, we're making our way from Hikairo straight up to the border

362
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,340
There are two big rivers that blow into each other there, is that right?

363
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,340
Yeah

364
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,340
I don't see any people though

365
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:49,340
Well...

366
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:53,340
This is proof that we're still on their trail at least

367
00:19:57,340 --> 00:20:00,340
Hey, you're not letting what that kid said bug you, right?

368
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,340
Oh, come on Magna, do I look like I'm upset?

369
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,340
Yeah, you do

370
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,340
How do I put this?

371
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:14,340
That poor kid's really struggling with his legs, so it makes sense that he would do anything to try and heal it, right?

372
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:17,340
And these devil believers are preying on that

373
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:21,340
Or at least pretending to be a ray of hope for people like him

374
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:25,340
These people have nowhere left to turn, they've run out of options

375
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:27,340
So we'll take a deal too good to be true

376
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:32,340
Yeah, well anyway, we've got to do something about them, fast

377
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:40,340
The area past Breed Mountain heading toward the Spade Kingdom has some volatile mana

378
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:42,340
The weather tends to get real rough

379
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:46,340
Odds are, they'll probably have to stop and wait it out

380
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:48,340
Roger that

381
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:50,340
There's backup on the way

382
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:53,340
But I want you three to race ahead and scout them out

383
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:56,340
We can't let them cross the border, understood?

384
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,340
Sir!

385
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:00,340
Nero

386
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:09,340
Oh crap!

387
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:11,340
Whoa!

388
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:14,340
Come on Magna, can't you fly this thing any steadier?

389
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:16,340
You're kidding me, right?

390
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:23,340
It's gonna be pretty difficult to catch them, if they manage to make it past Breed Mountain in this weather

391
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:26,340
Look down there, I think I see them!

392
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:28,340
Huh?

393
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:36,340
How are there so many? This is insane!

394
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:37,340
How are there so many? This is insane!

395
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,340
законnor

396
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:21,340
枕

397
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:34,340
OVER

398
00:22:34,340 --> 00:23:04,320
Thank you.

399
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:34,320
I'll see you next time.

400
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:40,420
We've finally caught up with them, and they really are heading to the Spade Kingdom.

401
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:43,180
Black Clover, page 147.

402
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:44,560
Prepared to die.

403
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:47,080
We can't wait for reinforcements!

404
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:48,220
Don't worry, Nero.

405
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:49,460
We'll save you!

